0929                         
0930                         ; The removal of energy from the main supply for the execution of 
0931                         ; commands, firing phasors and torpedoes, and moving through the 
0932                         ; galaxy is provided by the ELOM subroutine. The amount of energy 
0933                         ; to be removed is stored in the index register (as described in the 
0934                         ; ELOS subroutine) when the ELOM subroutine is called. If the main 
0935                         ; energy bank contains enough energy, the energy is deleted, and the 
0936                         ; subroutine returns to the calling program. If there is not enough 
0937                         ; energy, the shield energy is transferred to the main storage bank in 
0938                         ; an effort to provide for the loss. If this does not provide sufficient 
0939                         ; energy, the game is over. However, if the transfer does produce the 
0940                         ; energy needed in the main supply, the energy will be removed; and 
0941                         ; since the shield energy has been reduced to zero, an additional 25 
0942                         ; percent of the energy loss will be deleted from the main supply as a 
0943                         ; penalty.
0944                         
0945 081d 8d bd              ELOM        BSR         CKMN        ; Enough energy in main?
0946 081f 24 cc                          BCC         FMMN        ; Yes, take from main and return
0947 0821 de 26                          LDX         STORE1      ; No, save value of energy loss
0948 0823 df 2a                          STX         STORE3      ; Transfer shield energy and try again
0949 0825 7e 07 b7                       JMP         SDO1        ; 
0950                         
0951                         
0952                         ; The amount of energy transferred to or from the shields and the 
0953                         ; energy to be fired by the phasor is entered by the operator. The EIN 
0954                         ; subroutine is called to input these energy values. The first entry is 
0955                         ; checked to determine whether it is a minus sign, used in the shield 
0956                         ; entry. Location 55 on page 00 will be all zeros if the value is to be 
0957                         ; positive, and non-zero for a negative entry. Each digit entered is 
0958                         ; checked for validity, and then the ASCII code is masked off, resulting
0959                         ; in the BCD digits being stored in locations 54 through 51. The 
0960                         ; units digit is stored in location 51. Four digits must be entered by 
0961                         ; the operator when this routine is called. If the input is found to be 
0962                         ; invalid, the routine returns with the N flag set to T.’ If the input is 
0963                         ; valid, the N flag is reset upon returning to the calling program. 
0964                         
0965 0828 de 74              EIN         LDX         PDG5TH      ; Set pointer to start of digit store
0966 082a 6f 00                          CLR         0,X         ; Clear sign indicator 
0967 082c bd 0f 80                       JSR         INPUT       ; Get first character 
0968 082f 81 2d                          CMPA        #'-         ; Negative sign?  (was $AD)
0969 0831 26 05                          BNE         EN2         ; No, check digit 
0970 0833 a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; Make negative indicator not =0 
0971 0835 bd 0f 80           EN1         JSR         INPUT       ; Get next character 
0972 0838 09                 EN2         DEX                     ; Advance storage pointer 
0973 0839 a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; Store digit 
0974 083b bd 05 bd                       JSR         FNUM        ; Valid digit? 
0975 083e 2b 0a                          BMI         EIN1        ; No, return with N flag set 
0976 0840 a6 00                          LDAA        0,X         ; Yes, fetch digit 
0977 0842 84 0f                          ANDA        #$0F        ; Mask off ASCII bits 
0978 0844 a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; Save BCD value 
0979 0846 9c 72                          CPX         PDG1ST      ; End of input? 
0980 0848 26 eb                          BNE         EN1         ; No, fetch next digit 
0981 084a 39                 EIN1        RTS                     ; Yes, return 
0982                         
0983                         
0984                         ; When the space ship destroys an alien ship or space station, the 
0985                         ; result is the elimination of the alien ship or space station from the 
0986                         ; galaxy. The subroutine DLET is called to perform this function. 
0987                         ; First, the sector location of the object is cleared by storing a CO in 
0988                         ; the data table at the location indicated by the index register. From 
0989                         ; this location, the identity of the object to be deleted is ascertained. 
0990                         ; A pointer is then formed indicating the location of the quadrant in 
0991                         ; the galaxy content table from which the object is to be removed. If 
0992                         ; the object was a space station, it is removed from the galaxy and the 
0993                         ; number of space stations is decremented. If this value goes to zero, a 
0994                         ; warning message is output to inform the operator that the last space 
0995                         ; station has been destroyed. If an alien ship is destroyed, it is removed 
0996                         ; from the galaxy and its count is decremented. When the number of 
0997                         ; alien ships reaches zero, the game is over and the operator has successfully
0998                         ; completed the mission.
0999                         
1000 084b 86 c0              DLET        LDAA        #$C0        ; Load with clear character 
1001 084d a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; Clear object from table
1002 084f df 22                          STX         PNTR2       ; Save table location
1003 0851 96 4c                          LDAA        CQLSS       ; Get quadrant location
1004 0853 8b c0                          ADDA        #$C0        ; Form galaxy table pointer
1005 0855 bd 09 51                       JSR         ATINX1      ; Place pointer in index
1006 0858 df 24                          STX         PNTR3       ; Set table pointer
1007 085a de 22                          LDX         PNTR2       ; Fetch table location
1008 085c bd 09 59                       JSR         COMPAR      ; Space station hit? 
1009 085f 26 15                          BNE         DLAS        ; No, delete alien ship 
1010 0861 de 24                          LDX         PNTR3       ; Fetch galaxy pointer
1011 0863 a6 00                          LDAA        0,X         ; Get quadrant contents
1012 0865 84 37                          ANDA        #$37        ; Delete space station
1013 0867 a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; Restore quadrant in galaxy 
1014 0869 97 35                          STAA        CQC         ; Place new contents
1015 086b 7a 00 4e                       DEC         NSS         ; Decrement number of space stations
1016 086e 26 1b                          BNE         DLET1       ; If more left, return
1017 0870 ce 04 db                       LDX         #MSG37      ; If number of space stations =0,
1018 0873 7e 05 06                       JMP         MSG         ;  print warning message & return
1019                         
1020 0876 de 24              DLAS        LDX         PNTR3       ; Fetch galaxy pointer 
1021 0878 a6 00                          LDAA        0,X         ; Get quadrant contents
1022 087a 80 10                          SUBA        #$10        ; Delete 1 alien ship from quadrant
1023 087c a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; Restore to galaxy
1024 087e 97 35                          STAA        CQC         ; Save new contents
1025 0880 7a 00 4f                       DEC         NAS         ; Decrement number of alien ships 
1026 0883 26 06                          BNE         DLET1       ; More aliens, return
1027 0885 ce 03 d4                       LDX         #MSG27      ; All aliens destroyed!
1028 0888 7e 06 4d                       JMP         DONE        ; Print CONGRATULATIONS,
1029 088b 39                 DLET1       RTS                     ; Start new game
