1031                         
1032                         ; The final group of subroutines to be presented deals with the 
1033                         ; movement of the space ship through the galaxy, and the tracking of 
1034                         ; the torpedo within the quadrant. Moving an object through the 
1035                         ; galaxy is performed with the use of a table referred to as the 
1036                         ; COURSE TABLE. The course table, presented next, is located at the 
1037                         ; beginning of page 00, and contains 16 pairs of row and column dis¬ 
1038                         ; placement values. There is one pair of displacement values for each 
1039                         ; possible direction of movement. The first value of each pair is the 
1040                         ; column displacement; the second value is the row displacement. 
1041                         ; The entries in the course table are made up of the binary values 2, 1, 
1042                         ; 0, -1, and -2. A displacement of 1 advances the object one half of a 
1043                         ; sector for each sector move made. So, for example, if the course was 
1044                         ; chosen as 8.5, the displacement value for the column is two, and for 
1045                         ; the row is one. This means that for every column moved to the right, 
1046                         ; the object would move one half of a row down. A move is made by 
1047                         ; the program by separating the row and column location of the object 
1048                         ; to be moved, rotating each to the left once, and using the adjusted 
1049                         ; values to calculate the move. Then, for each sector move made, the 
1050                         ; row and column displacement is added to the adjusted row and 
1051                         ; column location. When the move is completed, the adjusted values 
1052                         ; are rotated to the right once, and then combined to give a new sector 
1053                         ; location to the object. By using this method it is possible for the 
1054                         ; direction of travel to be broken down to every 22 l A degrees. 
1055                         
1056                         ;---
1057                         
1058                         ; The subroutine DRCT is called to input the course direction from 
1059                         ; the operator through the input device. The two digits defining the 
1060                         ; move are checked for validity when entered, and then used to form a 
1061                         ; pointer to the course table. If the input is valid, the routine returns 
1062                         ; with the Z flag reset, and the pointer stored in location 20 on page 
1063                         ; 00. If invalid, the Z flag is set before returning. The ACTV subroutine
1064                         ; is then called to fetch the displacement values from the course 
1065                         ; table, and store the column displacement in location 2D and the row 
1066                         ; displacement in location 2C. It then sets up the adjusted row and 
1067                         ; column values, and stores them in locations 2E and 2F respectively. 
1068                         ;
1069                         ; The subroutine labeled TRK is called to make the individual sector
1070                         ; moves. First, the quadrant crossing flag is cleared. The column 
1071                         ; displacement is then added to the adjusted column location, and a 
1072                         ; quadrant crossing to the left or right is checked. If the crossing did 
1073                         ; occur, the crossing flag is set, and the adjusted column is corrected to 
1074                         ; indicate the new column value. The crossing is then checked for a 
1075                         ; move out of the galaxy, which would be indicated by the TRK subroutine
1076                         ; returning with the Z flag set. If the move is not out of the 
1077                         ; galaxy, the new quadrant location is stored at location 4C on page 
1078                         ; 00. The row displacement is then added to the adjusted row location, 
1079                         ; and a quadrant crossing up and down is checked. If a quadrant is 
1080                         ; crossed, the crossing flag is set and a move out of the galaxy is 
1081                         ; checked. If the crossing is out of the galaxy, the routine returns with 
1082                         ; the Z flag set. Otherwise, the new quadrant location is stored at location
1083                         ; 4C, and the routine returns with the Z flag reset. The final subroutine
1084                         ; of this group is called RWCM, and is called to restore the adjusted row
1085                         ; and column locations to the single byte used to define the 
1086                         ; final location of the object moved.
1087                         
1088                                     
1089 088c bd 0f 80           DRCT        JSR         INPUT       ; Input first course number 
1090 088f 81 31                          CMPA        #$31        ; Is input less than 1? (was $B1)
1091                         ;x        x BCS         ZRET        ; ***************replaced...        
1092 0891 2d 25                          BLT         ZRET        ; Yes, illegal input 
1093 0893 81 39                          CMPA        #$39        ; Is input greater than 8? (was $B9)
1094                         ;x        x BCC         ZRET        ; *************** replaced...
1095 0895 2c 21                          BGE         ZRET        ; Yes, illegal input 
1096 0897 84 0f                          ANDA        #$0F        ; No, mask off ASCII bits 
1097 0899 48                             ASLA                    ; If good times 2 
1098 089a 16                             TAB                     ; And save in B
1099 089b 86 2e                          LDAA        #'.         ; (was $AE)
1100 089d bd 0f 89                       JSR         PRINT       ; Print decimal point 
1101 08a0 bd 0f 80                       JSR         INPUT       ; Input second course number 
1102 08a3 81 30                          CMPA        #'0         ; Is digit zero? (was $B0)
1103 08a5 27 04                          BEQ         CR1         ; Yes, continue process 
1104 08a7 81 35                          CMPA        #'5         ; No, is digit =5? (was $B5)
1105 08a9 26 0d                          BNE         ZRET        ; No, return with Z flag set 
1106 08ab 84 01              CR1         ANDA        #$01        ; Mask off all but first bit 
1107 08ad 1b                             ABA                     ; Add first number input 
1108 08ae 48                             ASLA                    ; 
1109 08af 80 04                          SUBA        #$04        ; And form pointer to course table 
1110 08b1 97 21                          STAA        PNTR1+$1    ; Save pointer in temporary storage
1111 08b3 4f                             CLRA                    ;  
1112 08b4 97 20                          STAA        PNTR1       ; Clear least significant byte of pointer
1113 08b6 4c                             INCA                    ; Reset Z flag 
1114 08b7 39                             RTS                     ; Before returning 
1115 08b8 4f                 ZRET        CLRA                    ; Set Z flag 
1116 08b9 39                             RTS                     ; And return 
1117                         
1118 08ba 9f 22              ACTV        STS         PNTR2       ; Save stack pointer temporarily 
1119 08bc 9e 58                          LDS         PSTR51      ; Set stack to storage area 
1120 08be 96 36                          LDAA        SLOSS       ; Get present location 
1121 08c0 16                             TAB                     ; Save temporarily 
1122 08c1 c4 07                          ANDB        #$07        ; Mask out column 
1123 08c3 58                             ASLB                    ; Multiply by 2 
1124 08c4 37                             PSHB                    ; Store adjusted column 
1125 08c5 84 38                          ANDA        #$38        ; Mask out row 
1126 08c7 44                             LSRA                    ; 
1127 08c8 44                             LSRA                    ; Set up times 2 value 
1128 08c9 36                             PSHA                    ; Save adjusted row 
1129 08ca de 20                          LDX         PNTR1       ; Get displacement table pointer 
1130 08cc a6 00                          LDAA        0,X         ; Get column movement 
1131 08ce 36                             PSHA                    ; Store column displacement < 
1132 08cf a6 01                          LDAA        $01,X       ; Get row movement 
1133 08d1 36                             PSHA                    ; Store row displacement 
1134 08d2 9e 22                          LDS         PNTR2       ; Restore stack pointer
1135 08d4 39                             RTS                     ; 
1136                         
1137 08d5 7f 00 32           TRK         CLR         CF          ; Clear quadrant crossing flag 
1138 08d8 96 2f                          LDAA        STORE5+$1   ; Get adjusted column 
1139 08da 9b 2d                          ADDA        STORE4+$1   ; Add column move 
1140 08dc 97 2f                          STAA        STORE5+$1   ; Save temporarily current column 
1141 08de 2a 12                          BPL         NOBK        ; If no left crossing, branch 
1142 08e0 84 0f                          ANDA        #$0F        ; Left crossing correction 
1143 08e2 97 2f                          STAA        STORE5+$1   ; And save new adjusted column 
1144 08e4 7c 00 32                       INC         CF          ; Indicate left crossing 
1145 08e7 96 4c                          LDAA        CQLSS       ; And decrement current column 
1146 08e9 84 07                          ANDA        #$07        ; Is CQC =0? 
1147 08eb 27 56                          BEQ         TRK1        ; Yes, return with Z set 
1148 08ed 7a 00 4c                       DEC         CQLSS       ; No, decrement CQC 
1149 08f0 20 17                          BRA         RMV         ; Do row move 
1150                         
1151 08f2 81 10              NOBK        CMPA        #$10        ; Quadrant crossing right 
1152 08f4 25 13                          BCS         RMV         ; No, do row move 
1153 08f6 84 0f                          ANDA        #$0F        ; Yes, correct and 
1154 08f8 97 2f                          STAA        STORE5+$1   ; Save new adjusted column 
1155 08fa 7c 00 32                       INC         CF          ; Indicate crossing by making 
1156                         ;                                   ; Crossing flag non-zero 
1157 08fd 96 4c                          LDAA        CQLSS       ; Fetch current quadrant location 
1158 08ff 84 07                          ANDA        #$07        ; Separate column entry 
1159 0901 4c                             INCA                    ; Increment column entry 
1160 0902 81 08                          CMPA        #$08        ; Move out of galaxy 
1161 0904 27 3d                          BEQ         TRK1        ; Yes, return with flags set 
1162 0906 7c 00 4c                       INC         CQLSS       ; No, increment quadrant column 
1163                         
1164 0909 96 2e              RMV         LDAA        STORE5      ; Get adjusted row value 
1165 090b 9b 2c                          ADDA        STORE4      ; Add movement 
1166 090d 97 2e                          STAA        STORE5      ; Save new adjusted row 
1167 090f 2a 14                          BPL         NOUP        ; If not up, jump 
1168 0911 84 0f                          ANDA        #$0F        ; Move up one quadrant, correct 
1169 0913 97 2e                          STAA        STORE5      ; And save new adjusted value 
1170 0915 7c 00 32                       INC         CF          ; Make crossing flag non-zero 
1171 0918 96 4c                          LDAA        CQLSS       ; Decrement quadrant row 
1172 091a 16                             TAB                     ; Save temporarily 
1173 091b 84 38                          ANDA        #$38        ; Is quadrant row =0? 
1174 091d 27 24                          BEQ         TRK1        ; Yes, return with Z flag set 
1175 091f c0 08                          SUBB        #$08        ; No, decrement current quadrant row 
1176 0921 d7 4c                          STAB        CQLSS       ; Save new current quadrant 
1177 0923 20 1a                          BRA         CKX         ; Then perform crossing logic 
1178                         
1179                         
1180 0925 81 10              NOUP        CMPA        #$10        ; Quadrant crossing down? 
1181 0927 25 16                          BCS         CKX         ; No, check for crossing flag 
1182 0929 84 0f                          ANDA        #$0F        ; Yes, correct and 
1183 092b 97 2e                          STAA        STORE5      ; Save new adjusted row 
1184 092d 7c 00 32                       INC         CF          ; Indicate crossing 
1185 0930 96 4c                          LDAA        CQLSS       ; Then increment quadrant row
1186 0932 16                             TAB                     ; Save temporarily
1187 0933 84 38                          ANDA        #$38        ; Separate row entry
1188 0935 8b 08                          ADDA        #$08        ; Increment row value 
1189 0937 81 40                          CMPA        #$40        ; Out of galaxy?
1190 0939 27 08                          BEQ         TRK1        ; Yes, return with Z flag set
1191 093b cb 08                          ADDB        #$08        ; No, increment row
1192 093d d7 4c                          STAB        CQLSS       ; Save new current quadrant
1193                         
1194 093f 26 02              CKX         BNE         TRK1        ; Return with Z flag reset
1195 0941 86 01                          LDAA        #$01        ; If not, reset it
1196 0943 39                 TRK1        RTS                     ; 
1197                         
1198 0944 96 2f              RWCM        LDAA        STORE5+$1   ; Fetch adjusted column 
