1351                         
1352                         ; The next routine, which immediately follows the galaxy setup 
1353                         ; routine, is the short range scan. The location of each of the objects 
1354                         ; contained in the current quadrant is displayed as illustrated in the 
1355                         ; sample short range scan in Chapter One. By the use of the ROWSET, 
1356                         ; BINDEC, DIGPRT, and MSG subroutines, each line of the scan is 
1357                         ; prepared and output to the display device. This routine is entered 
1358                         ; following the galaxy setup to display the initial quadrant; then after 
1359                         ; each move by the space ship either within the quadrant or when a 
1360                         ; new quadrant is entered, and in response to a command to display 
1361                         ; a short range scan. 
1362                         
1363 0a65 ce 01 70           SRSCN       LDX         #MSG03      ; Set pointer for short range scan 
1364 0a68 bd 05 06                       JSR         MSG         ; Print initial row
1365 0a6b c6 01                          LDAB        #$01        ; Set row number one
1366 0a6d bd 06 76                       JSR         ROWSET      ; Set up row for printout
1367 0a70 86 32                          LDAA        #$32        ; 
1368 0a72 90 50                          SUBA        NSR         ; Calculate stardate number
1369 0a74 97 26                          STAA        STORE1      ; Save temporarily
1370 0a76 de 56                          LDX         PSTR1       ; Set pointer to binary value
1371 0a78 c6 01                          LDAB        #$01        ; Set precision counter
1372 0a7a bd 05 29                       JSR         BINDEC      ; Convert to current stardate 
1373 0a7d ce 01 b6                       LDX         #Msg05a+1   ; Set pointer to stardate message (was $01B6)
1374 0a80 c6 02                          LDAB        #$02        ; Set counter to number of digits 
1375 0a82 bd 06 62                       JSR         DIGPRT      ; Put digits in stardate message
1376 0a85 ce 01 a8                       LDX         #MSG05      ; Set pointer to message
1377 0a88 8d 24                          BSR         SRSCN1      ; Print stardate message
1378                         
1379 0a8a c6 02                          LDAB        #$02        ; Set row number two
1380 0a8c bd 06 76                       JSR         ROWSET      ; Set up row for printout
1381 0a8f 96 35                          LDAA        CQC         ; Fetch current quadrant contents
1382 0a91 ce 01 c3                       LDX         #Msg06a     ; Set pointer to condition message ( was $01C3 )
1383 0a94 84 30                          ANDA        #$30        ; Alien ship in quadrant? 
1384 0a96 26 19                          BNE         RED         ; Yes, condition red
1385 0a98 86 47                          LDAA        #'G        ; No, condition green (was $C7)
1386 0a9a a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; Fill in ‘GREEN’ in
1387 0a9c 86 52                          LDAA        #'R         ;  condition message  ( was $D2 )
1388 0a9e a7 01                          STAA        $01,X       ; 
1389 0aa0 86 45                          LDAA        #'E         ; (was $C5)
1390 0aa2 a7 02                          STAA        $02,X       ; 
1391                         ;x          LDAA        #'E         ; (was $C5)
1392 0aa4 01                             NOP                     ; 2nd E is
1393 0aa5 01                             NOP                     ;  Same as previous char, so no need to reload
1394 0aa6 a7 03                          STAA        $03,X       ; 
1395 0aa8 86 4e                          LDAA        #'N         ; (was $CE)
1396 0aaa a7 04                          STAA        $04,X       ; 
1397 0aac 20 11                          BRA         CND         ; Output condition message
1398 0aae 7e 05 06           SRSCN1      JMP         MSG         ; 
1399                         
1400 0ab1 86 52              RED         LDAA        #'R         ; Condition red (was $D2)
1401 0ab3 a7 00                          STAA        0,X         ; 
1402 0ab5 86 45                          LDAA        #'E         ; Fill in ‘RED’ in (was $C5)
1403 0ab7 a7 01                          STAA        $01,X       ;  condition message 
1404 0ab9 86 44                          LDAA        #'D         ; (was $C4)
1405 0abb a7 02                          STAA        $02,X       ; 
1406 0abd 6f 03                          CLR         $03,X       ; 
