1766                         
1767                         ; The torpedo routine fires a torpedo in the direction specified by 
1768                         ; the operator in an attempt to destroy an alien ship. This routine first 
1769                         ; checks the number of torpedoes available. If there are no torpedoes 
1770                         ; remaining, a message in output to inform the operator, and the routine
1771                         ; returns to the command routine. If there is a torpedo available, 
1772                         ; the torpedo count is decremented, and 250 units of energy are depleted
1773                         ; from the main storage bank. The DRCT subroutine is then 
1774                         ; called to input the direction of fire for the torpedo. The ACTV subroutine
1775                         ; then sets the adjusted row and column values for tracking the torpedo. 
1776                         ;
1777                         ; Once the trajectory is set up, the torpedo is moved one sector at 
1778                         ; a time, using the TRK subroutine. If the torpedo moves out of the 
1779                         ; quadrant, it has missed its intended target and the alien ship retaliates
1780                         ; by firing 200 units of phasor energy back at the space ship. 
1781                         ; Otherwise, the sector location of the torpedo is output in the tracking
1782                         ; message so that the operator can follow the torpedo’s path. The 
1783                         ; MATCH subroutine checks for a collision after each sector 
1784                         ; moved. If there is no collision at this sector, the torpedo will be 
1785                         ; tracked another sector by returning to the TR2 label in this routine. 
1786                         ; If an alien ship has been hit, it is removed from the galaxy. If it is 
1787                         ; the last alien ship, the mission is complete, and the program begins a 
1788                         ; new game. If a space station is hit, it is eliminated and the alien ship 
1789                         ; will retaliate as mentioned above. If a star is hit, the torpedo has 
1790                         ; missed its mark and the alien ship will again retaliate for the 
1791                         ; attempted attack. The program then returns to the command input 
1792                         ; routine.
1793                         
